# Headless clock-keeper test: clock-keeper-check asks a probe kernel
# (CLOCK_STALL_PROBE=1) to keep CPU 0's timer from its clock work, then times
# a receive deadline, a futex deadline and msTicks meanwhile: the other CPUs
# keep the system's time (Time.clockTick, Timekeeping_Turns).
(startup v1
  (start "logstore.svc" (priority 5) (test-console approve-declared))
  (start "clock-keeper-check.app" (priority 3))
)
